Package: emplikDTA
Type: Package
Title: Empirical Likelihood Inference for Diagnostic Test Accuracy
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    c(person(given = "Duc-Khanh",
           family = "To",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "tdkhanh@hcmus.edu.vn",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-4641-0764")),
           person(given = "Gianfranco",
                      family = "Adimari",
                      role = "ctb"),
               person(given = "Monica",
                      family = "Chiogna",
                      role = "ctb"))
Description: Estimates diagnostic accuracy for continuous markers in two or
    three independent ordered groups. Provides empirical receiver operating
    characteristic (ROC) curves and surfaces, empirical likelihood inference
    for the area under the curve and the volume under the surface, and
    kernel-based selection of diagnostic thresholds. Three-class empirical
    likelihood methods are described in To, Adimari, and Chiogna (2024)
    <doi:10.1177/09622802241238998>.
